Scenario: Retail Order Discount and Final Billing Calculation

A retail company wants to automate its billing process using PySpark. Students must create a Python UDF that calculates the final payable amount based on product category, purchase amount, quantity, and customer membership.
Input DataFrame
Order ID	Customer	Category	Unit Price (₹)	Quantity	Membership
101	Ravi	Electronics	25,000	2	Gold
102	Priya	Fashion	3,000	5	Silver
103	Arun	Groceries	1,500	10	Regular
104	Sneha	Electronics	60,000	1	Platinum
105	Kiran	Furniture	15,000	3	Gold
106	Meena	Fashion	2,500	4	Regular

Business requirements
Students must create a function named calculate_final_bill() implementing the following rules.
Condition	Discount
Electronics	10%
Fashion	15%
Groceries	5%
Furniture	8%
Gold membership	Additional 5%
Silver membership	Additional 3%
Platinum membership	Additional 10%
Regular membership	No additional discount

Calculation rules: First calculate unit_price × quantity. Apply the category discount, then apply the membership discount to the remaining amount. Return the final payable amount rounded to two decimal places.
